According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [65ae18af7a738b26]. In the input fence[ A ] B, the code fence holds object A, so A is the scored object. Object B appears after the closing fence but is not scored because the fence holds an object. In the rewritten text, object A is removed from inside the code fence, leaving it empty. The fence no longer holds an object, so the rule falls back to 'the last top-level object in the text', which is object B outside the fence. Thus the recovered object moves from {"a": 1} to {"b": 2}.